In this paper, we provide results about the nonwindowed scattering transform, which we formulate as the $q$ norm of a cascade of wavelet transforms and nonlinearities. The main result of this paper is a well-defined weighted measure with diffeomorphism stability properties akin to what is seen in the seminal paper, Group Invariant Scattering.

## Errata

An [errata (PDF)](/files/nonwindowed_scattering_errata.pdf), keyed to the arXiv version, is available. One statement changes: Theorem 6, and the results that depend on it, holds for one layer. For two or more layers the $q = 1$ scattering norm is infinite unless the scale measure is damped, and the errata states and proves the damped replacement. The remaining items are corrections to proofs that leave their statements intact, along with typos.

